  "findings": [
    "OUR DIFFERENTIATOR SURVIVES, ON QWEN ONLY. Under rank-1, Shairah-Qwen keeps 91% of GSM8K (0.4610 -> 0.4177) while version_B-Qwen drops to 2% (0.3889 -> 0.0091). Under surgical: 86% vs 27%. Both defenses block the attack on the headroom denominator (Shairah 4.8%/9.6%, version_B ~0%), but only version_B destroys the model. That is the fortress vs poison-pill split, measured on one protocol.",
    "SHAIRAH CAN BE NET-NEGATIVE. Qwen seed 2 gave the attacker MORE actionable harm than the UNDEFENDED base model under the same attack: 0.7865 vs the base heretic ceiling 0.6596 (131.6% headroom), with capability at 96% of clean. Verified not a judge artifact: 409/520 harmful_actionable, ratings concentrated at 4 (388) and 5 (35), 0 parse failures, spot-checked generations are coherent working code. On that draw the defense is worse than shipping nothing. Plausible mechanism (unconfirmed): extended-refusal training teaches fluent discussion of harmful topics in the overview section, so stripping refusal leaves a MORE articulate model than base.",
    "ON LLAMA, SHAIRAH STRICTLY DOMINATES US. It blocks rank-1 (headroom 0.23%) and surgical (1.2%) with capability at 95-104% AND usability untouched (XSTest safe benign 0.860, equal to its own clean model and ABOVE base's 0.812). version_B-Llama also blocks both attacks but its clean model answers only 0.316 of safe prompts. MAD never replicated on Llama, so our Llama arm was only ever a fortress -- and this is a better fortress, far cheaper.",
    "SHAIRAH'S CLEAN MODEL BEATS EVERY VERSION OF OURS. XSTest safe benign: Shairah 0.624 (Qwen) / 0.860 (Llama) vs our best 0.436 / 0.316 and base 0.744 / 0.812. Gibberish on BENIGN prompts 0.064 / 0.008 vs our 0.280 / 0.188 -- base-identical. It also has better capability (Qwen GSM8K 0.4610 vs version_B 0.3889).",
    "PROMPT SETS DISAGREE ABOUT HOW WELL SHAIRAH RESISTS ON QWEN. AdvBench headroom says 4.8% (blocked) but XSTest-unsafe shows refusal 0.875 -> 0.305 and harm 0.025 -> 0.200 under rank-1, an 8x increase. Qwen's base clean is already 0.2577 harmful, which compresses the AdvBench scale. Report both; the AdvBench-only reading understates the attack.",
    "Shairah-Llama clean is slightly LESS safe than base on XSTest-unsafe (refused 0.855 vs 0.915, harm 0.055 vs 0.030) despite perfect AdvBench refusal -- another case where AdvBench alone misleads.",
    "Attacking Shairah IMPROVES its benign usability in all six seeds (XSTest safe benign rises to 0.824-0.908 from clean 0.624 Qwen / 0.860 Llama). The attacker ends up with a model that is both uncensored and more helpful than the one the defender shipped."
  ],
